  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "Duel play 3v2 – stop the shots",
  "description": "Three attackers take on two defenders and a goalkeeper in one half. Only the ball side is used – the area beyond the cones is out of play, which gives the defenders a side to push towards and makes the attackers finish from the ball side. The centre line does not need defending. Each attack starts with the ball at the attacker furthest back.\n\nThe focus is on defending: the defenders close down the ball carrier, take away time and space, and try to turn the attackers away from goal before they can shoot. The goalkeeper works together with the defenders. Keep the attacks short and swap roles after a few goes.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "The nearest defender goes straight at the ball carrier – the other one covers the space in front of goal."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Steer the ball carrier towards the boards and away from good shooting spots."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Try to turn the attacker so their back faces the goal."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "The goalkeeper talks and helps the defenders cover the right shots."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp5",
      "text": "Ask the players: which spaces were hard to find, and where did most shots come from?"
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
  "difficulty": 3,
